From d34309c37515a81e81c0902f24c917d1194fd3c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 14:53:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] ktranslate: implement LLDP neighbor walk

Walks lldpLocPortEntry (1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.3.7.1) first to build a
lldpLocalPortNum -> {subtype, id, desc} map, then lldpRemEntry
(1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.4.1.1) for the actual neighbors. Chassis id and port
id are decoded according to their subtypes (macAddress -> colon-hex,
networkAddress -> dotted-quad for IPv4, local/interfaceName -> string,
everything else -> printable-ASCII or hex fallback).

Local port resolution matches the LLDP local-port identifier against
the interface metadata already gathered in the same poll cycle:
interfaceName -> ifDescr, interfaceAlias -> ifAlias, macAddress ->
ifPhysAddress, with a generic lldpLocPortDesc -> ifDescr fallback for
subtypes we can't resolve directly. Neighbors we can't resolve still
surface with LocalIfName set to whatever the device exposed.

Adds parser unit tests covering interfaceName/macAddress resolution,
the description fallback, chassis id decoding, MAC formatting, and
LLDP+CDP merge behaviour.
---
 pkg/inputs/snmp/metadata/topology.go      | 332 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 pkg/inputs/snmp/metadata/topology_test.go | 190 +++++++++++++
